# Build context for ops/deploy/server.Dockerfile (the Rust frick-server image).
# The Dockerfile copies the tree and builds `-p frick-server`, which only needs
# the Cargo workspace (crates/, Cargo.*, rust-toolchain.toml). Prune everything
# else — above all target/, which otherwise bloats the context enormously.
.git
.DS_Store
classes.jar
*.log

# Rust build output (do NOT ship the local target dir into the build)
target
**/target

# Node / TS / native client tooling the server build never touches
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/.turbo
**/.vite
**/.gradle
**/.swiftpm

# The TS web client, native SDKs, and demo apps are not part of the server image.
apps
packages

# Local databases / blobs / coverage
frick.sqlite
**/*.sqlite
frick-blobs
coverage
